commit 0df08db40e7b3deac88504ec9725468270593c80
Author: Minxi Hou <houminxi@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 15 01:56:41 2026 -0400

    review-hardening: keep receipts and hold-resume honest across restarts and diffs
    
    Receipt filenames carry no diff identity, so a changed diff that
    restarted at cycle 1 overwrote the receipts an earlier diff had written;
    the continuation index now resumes past the highest cycle on disk for
    any diff. Non-string excerpt content was laundered through str(), which
    turned a missing excerpt into the string "None" and passed schema
    validation as if a reviewer had written it; it now stays unconverted so
    the schema rejects the receipt. An excerpt whose content outruns its
    declared line range, or whose lines fall outside the diff post-image,
    previously skipped verification silently; both are now rejected, since
    a fabricated tail must not ride along unchecked. A one-line excerpt can
    coincide with a shifted position, so it is no longer eligible for the
    misnumbering diagnosis that needs at least two lines to convict.
    
    The hold-resume loop broke in the other direction: the cost-line change
    shorted it with a bare if True, so a LOCAL run ending PENDING returned
    without entering the HOLD prompt; the return is gated on PENDING again
    while the cost line still prints for it, since a PENDING run spends
    tokens like any other.
    
    The no-backend guard in the daemon-state axis also moved to just before
    its LLM call, so heuristic and static-rule checks still run when no
    backend is configured, and an early runtime-axis exit now clears its
    surfaces so the daemon-state axis never reuses the previous run's
    stale ones. The tests for the old restart behavior are re-contracted
    to the new one.
    
    Signed-off-by: Minxi Hou <houminxi@gmail.com>

